  <Program_Descriptions>
    <English>
      <Keywords>subtitle editor, authoring tool, java</Keywords>
      <Char_Desc_45>Subtitle editor and authoring tool</Char_Desc_45>
      <Char_Desc_80>Open source subtitle authoring, editing and correcting tool</Char_Desc_80>
      <Char_Desc_250>Jubler is an open source tool to edit text-based subtitles. It can be used as an authoring software for new subtitles or as a tool to convert, transform, correct and refine existing subtitles. Preview and spell checking is supported.</Char_Desc_250>
      <Char_Desc_450>Jubler is an open source tool to edit text-based subtitles. It can be used as an authoring software for new subtitles or as a tool to convert, transform, correct and refine existing subtitles. The most popular subtitle formats can be used. Preview of the subtitles in realtime or in design time, spell checking, translation mode and styles editing are some of the main features.</Char_Desc_450>
      <Char_Desc_2000>Jubler is a tool to edit text-based subtitles. It can be used as an authoring software for new subtitles or as a tool to convert, transform, correct and refine existing subtitles. The most popular subtitle formats can be used. Preview of the subtitles in realtime or in design time, spell checking, translation mode and styles editing are some of the main features.

Requirements are: latest version of JRE, MPlayer to view subtitles, ASpell to spell-check the subtitles.

It is free and open source software licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3 (AGPL-3.0). It is written in Java 8 in order to be really multi-platform. It has been tested under Linux, Windows, and macOS</Char_Desc_2000>
    </English>
  </Program_Descriptions>
